  "style": {
    "name": "Monsoon-coast Mughal jewel-box (azure-amber complementary)",
    "rationale": "Held the lapis/gold/quartz/crimson hierarchy and Taj massing, but killed every flat field: niche columns now read as recessed panels in gold ogee frames, the wide top band is broken into mulled lapis panels with crimson rosettes between gold pilasters, three continuous gold string-courses (y18/27/33) stop any tall field rising unbroken, the iwan is recessed 5 deep with a quartz pointed-arch ring and quartz door, the dome belly overhangs its drum by 2 per side, and minarets are engaged to the corners with quartz pinstripes and gold balcony rings — all relief from depth and shadow in the same four blocks, no new materials."
